  "prompt": "Pricing wants to see which sales of the April promotions' products were made on promotion. Take the products of the promotions that started in April 2025 (start_date from 1 to 30 April 2025), and their sales lines from 3 to 10 April 2025 (both days included). Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. For each line, show price_type: 'promo' when the line carries a promotion in order_lines.promo_id, and 'full price' when its promo_id is missing. List each line once, even for a product in two such promotions. Return five columns, in this order: order_line_id, product_id, order_date, units and price_type. Return one row for each line. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "order_line_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "product_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "order_date",
        "type_class": "temporal"
      },
      {
        "name": "units",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "price_type",
        "type_class": "text"
      }
    ],
    "grain": "one row per sales line of those products from 3 to 10 April 2025"
  },
